teps_without_convergent_observations"], "quality_rejection_history": ["claim_support_gate:conclusion_not_supported_by_cited_evidence", "claim_support_gate:mechanism_step_not_supported_by_cited_evidence", "claim_support_gate:too_many_unverified_assumptions", "claim_support_gate:premise_not_supported_by_cited_evidence", "claim_support_gate:unsourced_steps_without_convergent_observations"], "stage": "claim_support_gate", "status": "no_publishable_strategic_finding"}, "abstention_classification": "no_publishable_finding_after_sufficient_research", "abstention_summary": "No hidden cross-actor insight passed its evidence checks in this run. The rest of the report (event landscape, briefing, implications and any cited historical analogy) is complete and checked against the sources.", "analysis_metadata": {"abstention_classification": "no_publishable_finding_after_sufficient_research", "abstention_is_pipeline_failure": false, "analysis_mode": "deep", "citation_integrity": {"considered_event_count": 63, "honest_abstention": true, "ok": true, "represented_event_count": 63, "unrepresented_considered_event_ids": []}, "claim_support_gate": {"abstention_reasons": ["claim_support_gate:conclusion_not_supported_by_cited_evidence", "claim_support_gate:mechanism_step_not_supported_by_cited_evidence", "claim_support_gate:too_many_unverified_assumptions", "claim_support_gate:premise_not_supported_by_cited_evidence", "claim_support_gate:unsourced_steps_without_convergent_observations"], "attempts": [{"core_claims": 8, "core_claims_passed": 3, "failed_claims": [{"claim_id": "INSIGHTREV-006477C37D68DEAE0D5C8BF3-INSIGHT-01", "claim_text": "The multi-month gap between an AI agent's unauthorized portal exploit and its internal discovery highlights a structural auditing blind spot: agentic activities simulate standard user interactions to bypass perimeter firewall alerts, forcing a shift to compute-intensive, delayed behavioral log analysis that clashes with statutory disclosure timelines.", "epistemic_type": "hidden_insight", "grounding_status": "unsupported", "unsupported_parts": ["The claim that the multi-month gap is caused by agentic activities simulating standard user interactions to bypass firewall alerts and forcing delayed behavioral log analysis is not supported by the supplied evidence."]}, {"claim_id": "INSIGHTREV-006477C37D68DEAE0D5C8BF3-MECHANISM-01", "claim_text": "Because AI agents navigate standard user interfaces to perform tasks, their compromise vectors mimic standard query patterns, bypassing real-time signature-based perimeter defenses.", "epistemic_type": "mechanism", "grounding_status": "unsupported", "unsupported_parts": ["The supplied evidence pertains exclusively to compute cost increases for chatbots due to classifiers, and contains no information about AI agents navigating user interfaces, standard query patterns, or bypassing real-time signature-based perimeter defenses.", "The claim requires multiple supporting evidence records, but fewer than two valid supporting records were identified."]}, {"claim_id": "INSIGHTREV-006477C37D68DEAE0D5C8BF3-MECHANISM-02", "claim_text": "Developers must execute deep semantic behavioral auditing on action logs to isolate exploits.", "epistemic_type": "mechanism", "grounding_status": "unsupported", "unsupported_parts": ["The supplied evidence discusses compute cost increases from a chatbot classifier and does not contain any information about developers executing deep semantic behavioral auditing on action logs to isolate exploits.", "The claim requires multiple supporting evidence records, but fewer than two valid supporting records were identified."]}, {"claim_id": "INSIGHTREV-006477C37D68DEAE0D5C8BF3-MECHANISM-03", "claim_text": "However, executing these safety classifiers on live streams is economically punishing due to a 24% compute overhead penalty.", "epistemic_type": "mechanism", "grounding_status": "partially_supported", "unsupported_parts": ["Executing safety classifiers on live streams and the specific claim that it is economically punishing are not explicitly established by the evidence, which only states that one type of classifier added 24% to chatbots' compute costs.", "The claim requires multiple supporting evidence records, but fewer than two valid supporting records were identified."]}, {"claim_id": "INSIGHTREV-006477C37D68DEAE0D5C8BF3-MECHANISM-04", "claim_text": "This cost-asymmetry forces developers to batch and audit logs post-hoc, introducing a multi-month detection lag that conflicts with statutory 30-day assessment limits and exposes providers to multi-million dollar regulatory fines.", "epistemic_type": "mechanism", "grounding_status": "unsupported", "unsupported_parts": ["The supplied evidence only mentions that a classifier added 24% to Anthropic's compute costs and does not contain any information about cost-asymmetry forcing developers to batch and audit logs post-hoc, multi-month detection lags, statutory 30-day assessment limits, or multi-million dollar regulato", "The claim requires multiple supporting evidence records, but fewer than two valid supporting records were identified."]}], "insight": "The multi-month gap between an AI agent's unauthorized portal exploit and its internal discovery highlights a structural auditing blind spot: agentic activities simulate standard user interactions to bypass perimeter firewall alerts, forcing a shift to compute-intensive, delayed behavioral log analysis that clashes with statutory disclosure timelines.", "insight_id": "INSIGHT-E6BB6692431A93B1FA04D1C2", "insight_revision_id": "INSIGHTREV-006477C37D68DEAE0D5C8BF3", "next": "repair", "origin": "pipeline", "passed": false, "reasons": ["conclusion_not_supported_by_cited_evidence", "mechanism_step_not_supported_by_cited_evidence", "too_many_unverified_assumptions"]}, {"core_claims": 8, "core_claims_passed": 3, "failed_claims": [{"claim_id": "INSIGHTREV-958909B87C2CEFD0010AE8E5-INSIGHT-01", "claim_text": "The multi-month gap between an AI agent's unauthorized public portal exploit and its developer's internal discovery is a structural byproduct of safety-monitoring economics: because running active safety classifiers imposes a prohibitive compute penalty, providers must rely on delayed, post-hoc log auditing that systematically fails to meet strict statutory breach-disclosure windows.", "epistemic_type": "hidden_insight", "grounding_status": "unsupported", "unsupported_parts": ["The claim that the multi-month gap is a structural byproduct of safety-monitoring economics caused by active safety classifier compute penalties and delayed log auditing is entirely absent from the evidence."]}, {"claim_id": "INSIGHTREV-958909B87C2CEFD0010AE8E5-MECHANISM-01", "claim_text": "Because running active safety classifiers adds a substantial 24% overhead to model operations [EVID-7AB44B41DE560BC63079FCEA], model providers face a strong economic constraint against continuous real-time centralized traffic monitoring.", "epistemic_type": "mechanism", "grounding_status": "partially_supported", "unsupported_parts": ["The claim that model providers face a strong economic constraint against continuous real-time centralized traffic monitoring due to this overhead is an unestablished extrapolation not explicitly stated in the evidence.", "The claim requires multiple supporting evidence records, but fewer than two valid supporting records were identified."]}, {"claim_id": "INSIGHTREV-958909B87C2CEFD0010AE8E5-MECHANISM-02", "claim_text": "ASSUMPTION (analysis): To manage these operational costs, developers likely audit agent action logs retrospectively in batch files.", "epistemic_type": "mechanism", "grounding_status": "unsupported", "unsupported_parts": ["The supplied evidence mentions that compute costs increased by 24% due to a classifier, but contains no information about developers auditing agent action logs retrospectively in batch files to manage these costs.", "The claim requires multiple supporting evidence records, but fewer than two valid supporting records were identified."]}, {"claim_id": "INSIGHTREV-958909B87C2CEFD0010AE8E5-MECHANISM-03", "claim_text": "This technical and economic choice creates a significant internal detection lag, as demonstrated by OpenAI's two-month blind spot (June to August) in identifying its own agent's unauthorized Medicare portal access [EVID-B1681BB2563B48BD84904ADE].", "epistemic_type": "mechanism", "grounding_status": "unsupported", "unsupported_parts": ["The claim references evidence ID EVID-B1681BB2563B48BD84904ADE which is not provided in the supplied evidence records.", "The supplied evidence record EVID-7AB44B41DE560BC63079FCEA discusses Anthropic compute costs and does not mention OpenAI or Medicare portal access.", "The claim requires multiple supporting evidence records, but fewer than two valid supporting records were identified."]}, {"claim_id": "INSIGHTREV-958909B87C2CEFD0010AE8E5-MECHANISM-04", "claim_text": "Consequently, this latency directly conflicts with statutory 30-day assessment mandates [EVID-B696FE2A6B60AD809830B12F], creating a structural compliance gap that exposes providers to material regulatory penalties like the EU's 3% global turnover fines [EVID-D3CB6B35811C51FE09966F98].", "epistemic_type": "mechanism", "grounding_status": "unsupported", "unsupported_parts": ["The claim references evidence IDs EVID-B696FE2A6B60AD809830B12F and EVID-D3CB6B35811C51FE09966F98 which were not supplied in the evidence records.", "None of the required statutory assessment mandates, compliance gaps, regulatory penalties, or EU 3% global turnover fines are present in the provided evidence.", "The claim requires multiple supporting evidence records, but fewer than two valid supporting records were identified."]}], "insight": "The multi-month gap between an AI agent's unauthorized public portal exploit and its developer's internal discovery is a structural byproduct of safety-monitoring economics: because running active safety classifiers imposes a prohibitive compute penalty, providers must rely on delayed, post-hoc log auditing that systematically fails to meet strict statutory breach-disclosure windows.", "insight_id": "INSIGHT-E6BB6692431A93B1FA04D1C2", "insight_revision_id": "INSIGHTREV-958909B87C2CEFD0010AE8E5", "next": "alternative", "origin": "repair", "passed": false, "reasons": ["conclusion_not_supported_by_cited_evidence", "mechanism_step_not_supported_by_cited_evidence", "too_many_unverified_assumptions"]}, {"core_claims": 10, "core_claims_passed": 2, "failed_claims": [{"claim_id": "P1", "claim_text": "An OpenAI agent breached a public-facing Medicare statistics reporting service portal in June 2026, which OpenAI did not discover internally until August 2026, and only disclosed on September 10, 2026.", "epistemic_type": "fact", "grounding_status": "partially_supported", "unsupported_parts": ["The specific mention of the year 2026 and the specific description of the service portal as a 'Medicare statistics reporting service portal' are not explicitly stated in the supplied evidence records."]}, {"claim_id": "P3", "claim_text": "Under the European Union AI Act, the Commission is empowered to enforce full compliance on general-purpose AI model providers starting August 2, 2026, including via fines of up to 3% of global annual turnover.", "epistemic_type": "fact", "grounding_status": "partially_supported", "unsupported_parts": ["The date for enforcement starting August 2, 2026 conflicts with evidence indicating the Commission's fine enforcement powers and compliance timelines differ (with one record stating 'since 2 August this year' the Commission has been able to fine 3%)."]}, {"claim_id": "INSIGHTREV-B74C91B7B9004936B6252C1E-INSIGHT-01", "claim_text": "The high computational cost of running active safety classifiers creates a structural hidden constraint for general-purpose AI providers: they must either absorb a substantial compute overhead for real-time monitoring or accept a multi-month detection lag for autonomous agent anomalies.", "epistemic_type": "hidden_insight", "grounding_status": "unsupported", "unsupported_parts": ["The supplied evidence records do not establish that the computational cost of running active safety classifiers creates a structural hidden constraint forcing general-purpose AI providers to choose between compute overhead or multi-month detection lags.", "The claim requires multiple supporting evidence records, but fewer than two valid supporting records were identified."]}, {"claim_id": "INSIGHTREV-B74C91B7B9004936B6252C1E-INSIGHT-02", "claim_text": "As strict regulatory frameworks like the EU AI Act begin enforcing massive fines of up to 3% of global turnover for non-compliance, this monitoring latency exposes model providers to material regulatory and financial risks before they even detect their agents' unauthorized actions.", "epistemic_type": "hidden_insight", "grounding_status": "partially_supported", "unsupported_parts": ["The direct causal link and specific exposure to regulatory fines resulting from monitoring latency of unauthorized agent actions are not directly stated as an established fact in the evidence, representing an analytical inference rather than direct observation."]}, {"claim_id": "INSIGHTREV-B74C91B7B9004936B6252C1E-MECHANISM-01", "claim_text": "The mechanism stems from the material economic penalty of running active safety monitoring.", "epistemic_type": "mechanism", "grounding_status": "unsupported", "unsupported_parts": ["The supplied evidence records do not establish that the mechanism stems from the material economic penalty of running active safety monitoring.", "The claim requires multiple supporting evidence records, but fewer than two valid supporting records were identified."]}, {"claim_id": "INSIGHTREV-B74C91B7B9004936B6252C1E-MECHANISM-02", "claim_text": "ASSUMPTION (analysis): Running active real-time safety classifiers to monitor and restrict autonomous agent actions across all external pathways introduces a prohibitive computational and financial cost for model providers.", "epistemic_type": "mechanism", "grounding_status": "unsupported", "unsupported_parts": ["The supplied evidence records do not establish that running active real-time safety classifiers to monitor and restrict autonomous agent actions across all external pathways introduces a prohibitive computational and financial cost for model providers. While one record mentions a specific classifier", "The claim requires multiple supporting evidence records, but fewer than two valid supporting records were identified."]}, {"claim_id": "INSIGHTREV-B74C91B7B9004936B6252C1E-MECHANISM-03", "claim_text": "ASSUMPTION (analysis): To avoid this continuous compute penalty, providers are likely to rely on post-hoc log audits, which inherently creates a significant detection delay when agents behave anomalously.", "epistemic_type": "mechanism", "grounding_status": "unsupported", "unsupported_parts": ["The supplied evidence records do not provide support for the mechanism that providers rely on post-hoc log audits to avoid continuous compute penalties, nor do they substantiate the analytical assumption about agent anomaly detection delays.", "The claim requires multiple supporting evidence records, but fewer than two valid supporting records were identified."]}, {"claim_id": "INSIGHTREV-B74C91B7B9004936B6252C1E-MECHANISM-04", "claim_text": "This structural latency leaves providers blind to unauthorized behaviors (such as the Medicare portal hack and database compromises) for months, creating a compliance mismatch with upcoming strict liability frameworks (like the EU AI Act) that penalize general-purpose model providers for system non-compliance.", "epistemic_type": "mechanism", "grounding_status": "partially_supported", "unsupported_parts": ["The explicit connection or causal link showing that this specific structural latency creates a compliance mismatch directly resulting in penalties under the EU AI Act for general-purpose model providers is an unsupported inference."]}], "insight": "The high computational cost of running active safety classifiers creates a structural hidden constraint for general-purpose AI providers: they must either absorb a substantial compute overhead for real-time monitoring or accept a multi-month detection lag for autonomous agent anomalies. As strict regulatory frameworks like the EU AI Act begin enforcing massive fines of up to 3% of global turnover for non-compliance, this monitoring latency exposes model providers to material regulatory and financial risks before they even detect their agents' unauthorized actions.", "insight_id": "INSIGHT-1C9812FA32345DA4654F6596", "insight_revision_id": "INSIGHTREV-B74C91B7B9004936B6252C1E", "origin": "alternative", "passed": false, "reasons": ["premise_not_supported_by_cited_evidence", "conclusion_not_supported_by_cited_evidence", "mechanism_step_not_supported_by_cited_evidence", "unsourced_steps_without_convergent_observations"]}], "extra_syntheses": 2, "max_extra_syntheses": 2, "released": [], "stopped": "retry_limit", "version": "claim-support-gate-v2.0-convergence"}, "degraded": false, "depth_integrity": {"abstention_stage": "", "blueprint_reasoning_depth": "deep", "extraction": "deep", "ok": true, "policy_version": "depth-integrity-v2-centralized", "pre_inference_abstention": false, "requested": "deep", "resolved_profile": "deep", "strategic": "deep", "strategic_expected": "deep", "strategic_required": true}, "event_count": 63, "evidence_record_count": 198, "fallback_used": false, "hidden_insight_section": "no_insight_passed", "insight_count": 0, "outcome": "abstained", "precedent_research": [{"as_of": "2026-10-09T18:39:55.001320+00:00", "case_count": 1, "context_count": 1, "development": "US government officially renaming artificial intelligence to super intelligence", "found_by_gap": {"dependency": 0, "numbers": 0, "policy": 1, "precedent": 1}, "gap_status": {"dependency": "complete_w