indow", "strategic_topic_linkage_type", "strategic_topic_relevance_score", "summary", "temporal_precision", "temporal_status", "title", "underlying_event_id", "underlying_event_member_count", "updated_at"], "event_summary": "Three further incidents of rogue AI activity linked to OpenAI agents were also reported on Wednesday by research lab Transluce. The group, which describes itself as a \"nonprofit research lab dedicated to public oversight\" of AI, said it had identified evidence that OpenAI's systems had attempted to compromise websites linked to the University of New Mexico, the Australian Institute of Health and Welfare, and Data USA, a non-government platform that aggregates data from US government sources.", "raw_actor_fields": {"acting_entity": null, "actor": null, "company": null, "institution": null, "organisation": null, "organization": null, "primary_actor": null, "regulator": null}, "raw_entity_mentions": [{"entity_type": "organization", "mention": "Transluce", "raw_keys": ["context", "entity_type", "mention", "role", "sentence_id", "source_span", "type_source"], "role": "actor"}, {"entity_type": "unknown", "mention": "websites linked to the University of New Mexico, the Australian Institute of Health and Welfare, and Data USA", "raw_keys": ["context", "entity_type", "mention", "role", "sentence_id", "source_span", "type_source"], "role": "object"}], "resolved_primary_actor": "Transluce", "source_id": "SOURCE-50419A862D1E9782B95B8F0E"}, {"admission_reasons": [], "admission_status": "considered", "diagnostic_version": "strategic-actor-admission-diagnostics-v1", "entity_mentions_state": "present", "event_id": "EVENT-0242507B013C85729657D3F8", "event_keys": ["claim_status", "created_at", "entity_mentions", "event_date_precision", "event_dates_version", "event_end_at", "event_id", "event_start_at", "event_time_resolved", "event_time_text", "event_type", "extraction_metadata", "published_at", "quantitative_claims", "relationship_mentions", "snippets", "source_id", "strategic_admission_reasons", "strategic_admission_status", "strategic_cluster_check", "strategic_cluster_development", "strategic_cluster_id", "strategic_cluster_label", "strategic_cluster_status", "strategic_cluster_terms", "strategic_dependency_tags", "strategic_event_class", "strategic_geography", "strategic_materiality_score", "strategic_mechanism_tags", "strategic_relation_signature", "strategic_theme", "strategic_time_window", "strategic_topic_linkage_type", "strategic_topic_relevance_score", "summary", "temporal_precision", "temporal_status", "title", "underlying_event_id", "underlying_event_member_count", "updated_at"], "event_summary": "The European Union has required them since August 2025, and since 2 August this year the Commission has been able to fine a model provider 3% of worldwide turnover. Article 55 of the AI Act has obliged providers of general-purpose models with systemic risk to run adversarial testing, assess risk at union level and report serious incidents without undue delay since August 2025. The penalties arrived in August. Since the second of that month the Commission has been able to fine a provider up to 3% of worldwide annual turnover or EUR 15M, whichever is higher. It can demand access to a model, order evaluations and require a provider to restrict its public availability.", "raw_actor_fields": {"acting_entity": null, "actor": null, "company": null, "institution": null, "organisation": null, "organization": null, "primary_actor": null, "regulator": null}, "raw_entity_mentions": [{"entity_type": "organization", "mention": "Commission", "raw_keys": ["context", "entity_type", "mention", "role", "sentence_id", "source_span", "type_source"], "role": "actor"}, {"entity_type": "unknown", "mention": "model provider", "raw_keys": ["context", "entity_type", "mention", "role", "sentence_id", "source_span", "type_source"], "role": "object"}], "resolved_primary_actor": "Commission", "source_id": "SOURCE-522409DCAF21B3E9CFDA38B3"}, {"ad